==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|incongruus|lang=la}}, from {{term|in-|lang=la||not}} + {{term|lang=la|congruus||congruent}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈɪn.cɒn.ɡɹʊu.ʌs/}} ''or'' {{IPA|/ˈɪn.cɒŋ.ɹʊu.ʌs/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ɪnˈkɑn.ɡɹu.əs/}} ''or'' {{IPA|/ɪŋˈkɑŋ.ɡɹu.əs/}}
* {{audio|en-us-incongruous.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Not [[similar]] or [[congruent]]; not [[matching]] or [[fitting]] in.
#: ''The old camper looked a bit '''incongruous''' in an upscale neighborhood, but he enjoyed traveling in it.''

